000100 REM TRY / CATCH / THROW -- On Error Resume Next, with punctuation
      *
      * 1. THROW does not unwind. The line after it still runs. The handler
      *    runs too, because CATCH is bottom-tested, like WHILE.
       TRY
       PRINT "try: before the throw"
       THROW "boom"
       PRINT "try: after the throw (this line still runs)"
       CATCH
       PRINT "catch: handled " + $!
       ENDTRY
      *
      * 2. Nothing thrown. The handler still runs. $! holds whatever it held.
       TRY
       PRINT "try2: nothing thrown here"
       CATCH
       PRINT "catch2: ran regardless; $! is " + $!
       ENDTRY
      *
      * 3. A typed CATCH matches $! with loose == (PHP 5). The wrong type is
      *    skipped; the right one, eventually, is not.
       TRY
       THROW "teapot"
       CATCH "nope"
       PRINT "catch3a: this should not print"
       CATCH "teapot"
       PRINT "catch3b: caught the teapot"
       ENDTRY
      *
      * 4. An error raised while handling an error: the runtime shows you an
      *    unrelated stack trace, for humility (spec 5).
       TRY
       THROW "the first problem"
       CATCH
       THROW "the second problem, raised during cleanup"
       ENDTRY
      *
      * 5. THROW takes any value; a bare THROW re-raises $!.
       $reason = "disk full"                   ;
       TRY
       THROW $reason
       CATCH
       THROW
       ENDTRY
       FREE($reason)
      *
       PRINT "done"
